40:Use the existing `NativeResult`, `createIRArtifact`, `diff`, `makeCorrespondence` and `undeclaredWrites`. The narrow entry point has no manager-dependent analysis, preservation, edit or async callback. Type its gate to return a synchronous check result and require explicit success. Return identity candidates immediately. A synchronous general-purpose AnalysisManager would duplicate transaction semantics. A tensor-local runner could compose the same primitives, but would make the second domain own framework write and publication checks. Returning a Promise would change the stipulated API.
44:**Probe on the current worktree.** The baseline build succeeded. On Node 24.18.0 a minimal adapter and artifact passed a synchronous one-case differential check (`agree`). Applying a native identity pass returned a Promise and rejected with `Adapter t.probe is not Rewritable`. The diary gives the setup and numeric witness.
52:3. Match a plain RHS index to the corresponding axis of the tensor it reads. Unify all such extents symbolically, independent of term order. Match each LHS binder to its declared axis if present. Check inferred and declared extents agree. An affine-only LHS binder needs the annotation. A reduction binder has no annotation slot and needs a plain witness within scope. In a convolution, `dy` gets its extent from the kernel's `dy` axis and `y` from the result annotation. A product of two variable indices is non-affine.
64:| Generated reduction bounds | Block count by ceiling division and tail length by minimum. Only generated loop bounds need these operations. Tensor addresses stay affine. |
76:**Observation.** Compare the same named function's returned shape and every row-major element. Check names and signatures of all functions first. Exact means equal 32-bit output words, including zero sign, using Uint32Array views of f32 storage. Tolerance compares candidate f32 with origin f64 on the *same f32 input bits*. Use finite reference outputs for the tolerance sample domain, chosen from the origin alone. Candidate NaN or infinity for a finite reference fails. Report the first mismatch with coordinate, values/bit words and permitted error. Keep nonfinite evidence JSON-safe by using strings. The exact comparator can examine any f32 bits, including nonfinite results.
104:Build and test through the fixed public exports. Put focused tests in `tests/tensor/` for parsing and location errors, symbolic binding, affine-only axes, bad extents and duplicate assignments, max/call ambiguity, nested scope, signed zero, lexicographic multi-index folds, and per-operation rounding. Include a Float64Array input distinguishable from its f32 rounding. Verify unchanged source revision, multiple functions, pass order, repeat optimization, and acceptance and rejection using real changed artifacts, including both mutants through the actual gate. Run `npm run build`, `node --test tests/tensor/`, `node --test tests/framework/` and Typed pass/contract consumers (`passes`, `program`, `mutate`, `strategies` tests at minimum). Request escalation if a Node child-process test encounters sandbox EPERM.

